@startuml Sprint1_AddSkill_Sequence
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

title Sprint 1: Add Skill - MVC Sequence

actor User
participant "SkillsComponent\n(View)" as View
participant "SkillController\n(Controller)" as Controller
database "skills Table\n(Model)" as Model

== **Auth (See: Sprint1_Authentication_Sequence)** ==

rect rgb(220, 220, 220)
  User -> User: Verify JWT Token\n(auth guard + interceptor)
  note right of User: Referenced diagram:\nSprint1_Authentication_Sequence
end

== **Add Skill Flow** ==

User -> View: Enter skill name\n("Python")\nClick Add button
activate View

View -> Controller: POST /api/skills\n{data: {name: "Python"}}
activate Controller

Controller -> Model: INSERT INTO skills\n(name, created_at, updated_at)\nVALUES ('Python', NOW(), NOW())
activate Model

alt name is unique
    Model -> Controller: Success\n{id: 5, name: "Python", documentId: "xyz123..."}
    
else name already exists
    Model -> Controller: PostgreSQL ERROR\nUnique constraint violation
    Controller -> View: HTTP 409 Conflict\n{error: "Skill name already exists"}
    View -> User: Show error message
    stop
end

deactivate Model

Controller -> View: HTTP 201 Created\n{data: {id: 5, name: "Python", documentId: "xyz123..."}, meta: {...}}
deactivate Controller

View -> View: Add skill to this.skills array\nClear input field\nthis.newName = ""
View -> User: Display "Python" in skills list\nShow success message
deactivate View

@enduml
